WEBVTT

00:00.966 --> 00:04.966
Was hast Du am 7. Oktober erlebt?

00:06.966 --> 00:08.733
Wow...

00:09.533 --> 00:13.333
6:30 in the morning I woke up to the sound of alarms,

00:13.933 --> 00:16.300
which we are used to, unfortunately.

00:16.600 --> 00:19.066
We ran to the safe room,

00:19.233 --> 00:20.833
where my children sleep,

00:21.766 --> 00:23.666
me and my husband and the dogs,

00:23.733 --> 00:26.233
and we closed the door and we waited for it to finish.

00:26.566 --> 00:27.533
But it didn’t finish,

00:27.533 --> 00:30.500
it was unstoppable and it was very close.

00:30.500 --> 00:33.400
It was right in the neighborhoods where people live,

00:34.133 --> 00:35.733
and...

00:37.766 --> 00:41.000
I think that it was 20 minutes after that,

00:41.000 --> 00:42.866
that we turned the television on...

00:43.033 --> 00:48.000
And we saw the white pickup trucks in Sderot

00:48.333 --> 00:49.333
with the...

00:49.333 --> 00:50.733
the terrorists on them,

00:50.733 --> 00:53.933
and that moment I looked at it and I said

00:53.933 --> 00:54.633
"Oh my god"

00:54.633 --> 00:56.500
"If this is happening in Sderot",

00:56.500 --> 00:58.833
which is about 15 minutes drive from here,

00:58.933 --> 01:01.100
"What on earth is happening in my kibbutz?",

01:01.800 --> 01:02.900
and...

01:03.166 --> 01:04.266
there was...

01:04.833 --> 01:07.333
at that time there were already

01:07.333 --> 01:09.133
terrorists inside the kibbutz,

01:09.133 --> 01:10.600
but we didn’t know it.

01:11.133 --> 01:12.800
I live in the center of the kibbutz,

01:12.800 --> 01:15.400
and they entered through the back gate,

01:15.533 --> 01:18.733
to another neighborhood that was quite far from mine,

01:20.000 --> 01:22.000
and they started breaking in.

01:22.833 --> 01:25.900
One of the first places they came was here,

01:25.900 --> 01:28.200
to the dairy farm.

01:28.433 --> 01:31.833
There were two people working there that morning.

01:32.133 --> 01:33.600
Two students...

01:33.700 --> 01:35.700
lovely students from Tanzania.

01:36.000 --> 01:37.966
Every year Tanzania sends

01:37.966 --> 01:40.166
top students here,

01:40.166 --> 01:42.400
in order to learn agriculture,

01:42.400 --> 01:44.600
and bring it back to their country.

01:45.600 --> 01:47.700
Really amazing young people,

01:50.733 --> 01:52.833
Every time I speak about it I can’t...

01:55.000 --> 01:56.800
They came inside here,

01:57.333 --> 02:01.300
there were two students. One of them managed to

02:01.733 --> 02:05.433
run away, the other one was caught by Hamas.

02:05.833 --> 02:07.600
He was tortured and murdered

02:07.966 --> 02:10.500
and they took his body to the Gaza Strip.

02:10.900 --> 02:12.966
We first thought that he was only kidnapped,

02:12.966 --> 02:14.566
but then we realized that,

02:15.900 --> 02:16.933
they killed him.

02:17.700 --> 02:21.733
The father came all the way from Tanzania

02:21.733 --> 02:23.900
to take his son's body

02:23.900 --> 02:25.533
and they wouldn’t release the body,

02:25.533 --> 02:28.466
The body is still there for 2 years,

02:28.700 --> 02:31.100
his name was Joshua Luito Malal.

02:32.133 --> 02:33.600
Sweet, sweet boy.

02:35.800 --> 02:37.833
Then they ran

02:37.833 --> 02:40.833
to that direction over there.

02:40.833 --> 02:42.633
That's the neighborhood where

02:42.733 --> 02:45.833
the Thai people that work here in the kibbutz sleep.

02:46.133 --> 02:50.233
And they started running,

02:50.566 --> 02:52.266
into their...

02:55.566 --> 02:57.300
The Thai

02:57.300 --> 03:01.600
started running away. I'm sorry for the description,

03:01.600 --> 03:04.033
but one of them was caught and was killed,

03:04.033 --> 03:06.033
was murdered with a shovel.

03:08.100 --> 03:09.400
And the rest of them,

03:09.400 --> 03:11.400
there were a few more that were injured,

03:11.400 --> 03:13.333
the rest of them started running,

03:14.400 --> 03:16.366
carrying the injured, also,

03:16.366 --> 03:20.433
started running towards the neighborhood,

03:20.433 --> 03:22.400
that was next to them.

03:23.133 --> 03:26.300
There was one house in that neighborhood they rent to,

03:26.300 --> 03:28.033
that was two stories high,

03:28.400 --> 03:32.933
and there was a father there, his son,

03:33.133 --> 03:35.133
for Shabbat,

03:35.633 --> 03:37.166
He came from the army.

03:37.166 --> 03:38.500
He's in the army and he came,

03:38.766 --> 03:42.333
so he had a M16 in his

03:42.333 --> 03:44.700
House and he told his wife,

03:44.700 --> 03:47.466
he put his family in one of the safe rooms,

03:47.466 --> 03:48.766
and he told his wive:

03:48.766 --> 03:51.533
"Nobody will get near this neighborhood",

03:51.533 --> 03:54.900
"I will make sure that...", they had like a little

03:54.966 --> 03:57.233
mini neighborhood of five houses.

03:57.800 --> 04:01.600
He stands there and he sees the

04:02.233 --> 04:05.933
Thai people running towards the neighborhood,

04:07.566 --> 04:08.700
He runs down,

04:09.333 --> 04:12.733
he opens the door, he lets them all in,

04:12.733 --> 04:14.800
and he puts them with his family.

04:15.533 --> 04:20.100
And he goes back upstairs and started shooting

04:20.100 --> 04:21.466
the terrorists.

04:22.500 --> 04:25.400
My sister was his neighbor,

04:25.400 --> 04:28.200
her house was just in front of his.

04:28.900 --> 04:31.633
And my parents were also there that day,

04:31.633 --> 04:33.333
and it was a holiday,

04:33.333 --> 04:37.533
they came to visit and the lock of

04:37.533 --> 04:41.400
her safe room, the window was...

04:43.366 --> 04:45.866
was broken...

04:48.433 --> 04:51.233
My sister's safe room,

04:51.533 --> 04:54.466
the lock of the window was broken,

04:54.900 --> 04:59.066
and one of the terrorists spots it from outside.

04:59.633 --> 05:04.066
And they start running towards my sister's window

05:04.066 --> 05:07.700
and there started a battle.

05:08.100 --> 05:13.433
On one side it was my brother in law, holding

05:13.766 --> 05:16.333
the shutters, and on the other side,

05:16.333 --> 05:18.600
there were the terrorists trying to open it.

05:18.700 --> 05:21.600
I was with them on the phone at the same time,

05:21.700 --> 05:25.300
and I could hear the screaming of my nephews,

05:25.900 --> 05:27.300
and...

05:27.366 --> 05:28.400
I can hear that there's,

05:28.400 --> 05:33.700
and then I hear shooting. Their neighbor Ran Poslushni,

05:34.733 --> 05:38.933
the sweet, sweet Ran that we always remember as a true hero,

05:39.533 --> 05:44.400
he shot them and saved my family.

05:45.633 --> 05:47.333
At a certain point,

05:47.333 --> 05:48.433
that day

05:48.433 --> 05:52.533
Ran was shot and killed and

05:52.533 --> 05:54.700
This brave man managed to save

05:55.900 --> 06:01.000
approximately 40 people before he before he died.

06:01.766 --> 06:05.233
Before he was murdered.

06:06.300 --> 06:08.866
A very sad story.

06:10.133 --> 06:12.900
Because I was head of education,

06:12.900 --> 06:14.966
there were a few teenagers

06:14.966 --> 06:17.600
that felt comfortable speaking to me.

06:18.533 --> 06:22.833
And the teenagers that day went through really

06:22.833 --> 06:24.733
difficult

06:24.733 --> 06:26.633
situations because

06:26.933 --> 06:29.900
You’re not a child anymore,

06:29.966 --> 06:31.500
you’re not a grown up anymore,

06:31.500 --> 06:35.400
but people trust you to do things so...

06:36.233 --> 06:38.200
some of them really

06:38.566 --> 06:40.900
had to take care of entire families.

06:41.700 --> 06:44.300
I'm going to read you a very small part

06:44.433 --> 06:47.033
of a very long texting

06:47.033 --> 06:50.266
between me and a fourteen-and-half year old

06:52.133 --> 06:54.900
brave, brave, brave girl.

06:56.233 --> 07:00.133
This girl started texting me

07:02.100 --> 07:05.733
around 7:45 in the morning and

07:05.733 --> 07:08.433
this texting finished around 11 at night,

07:08.433 --> 07:09.666
it’s so long.

07:10.800 --> 07:12.533
I'm not going to read it all of course,

07:12.533 --> 07:15.100
because it kinds of repeats itself also.

07:16.566 --> 07:18.166
She started texting me at

07:18.166 --> 07:19.900
A 7:45 in the morning,

07:20.866 --> 07:22.566
and...

07:22.766 --> 07:24.500
I was in a different neighborhood,

07:24.500 --> 07:28.400
so we were experiencing a whole different scenario.

07:29.000 --> 07:33.566
I'm going to read it from the middle.

07:40.166 --> 07:42.800
This is 9:45 in the morning.

07:45.666 --> 07:49.133
This girl is with her mother and her younger brother

07:49.400 --> 07:52.700
in their house. The mother is paralyzed with fear.

07:53.566 --> 07:55.233
The older brother,

07:55.233 --> 07:56.766
who's about 18

07:56.766 --> 07:58.866
is in another neighborhood of the kibbutz,

07:58.866 --> 08:00.333
he has his own unit.

08:01.700 --> 08:06.666
And, she starts crying for help.

08:07.100 --> 08:11.733
Straight in the morning this is 9:45.

08:12.033 --> 08:14.800
"I hear them right outside my house",

08:14.833 --> 08:17.166
"they are shouting, they are shooting"

08:17.300 --> 08:18.966
"Please someone come help"

08:18.966 --> 08:21.966
"they are shouting and shooting outside my house"

08:21.966 --> 08:25.066
"we must keep quiet they are shouting again",

08:25.066 --> 08:29.000
"I'm scared as Oshrit. I'm almost out of battery"

08:30.366 --> 08:31.466
I start

08:31.466 --> 08:35.633
trying to calm her down and I tell her to

08:35.633 --> 08:39.166
close all the apps in the background to save battery.

08:39.666 --> 08:41.833
"Oh my God they are shouting right here"

08:41.833 --> 08:44.466
"Oh my God, Oshrit, they are right here outside my house",

08:44.466 --> 08:46.000
"I can really hear them"...

08:48.466 --> 08:53.200
I tell her, 09:50 am,

08:53.433 --> 08:55.700
I tell her "breathe, honey".

08:55.833 --> 09:00.400
"The army is patrolling, I am sure that the IDF is here"

09:00.400 --> 09:01.900
Because who would have thought...

09:03.566 --> 09:05.066
"Please send someone"

09:05.633 --> 09:07.800
"Please send someone, they are shooting",

09:07.800 --> 09:10.000
"Please send someone now".

09:10.000 --> 09:13.566
Now look at the how resourceful she was.

09:13.833 --> 09:17.000
The phone of her mother was out of battery,

09:17.400 --> 09:19.633
and in many of the neighborhoods,

09:19.633 --> 09:22.800
there was no electricity nor communication.

09:22.800 --> 09:24.933
Many of the...

09:30.633 --> 09:32.266
How do you say that?

09:33.800 --> 09:36.433
Many of the infrastructures

09:36.433 --> 09:38.133
were damaged that day.

09:39.366 --> 09:41.933
So, her mom didn’t have a phone,

09:42.233 --> 09:44.166
and as I told you before,

09:44.166 --> 09:47.933
Us, the adults, we get the security messages to our phones.

09:48.366 --> 09:52.133
so she asks me to send every message to her phone,

09:52.200 --> 09:54.466
so she will know what was going what's going on.

09:57.000 --> 09:59.166
09:57 am

09:59.300 --> 10:03.833
"Oshrit, he's right here he's shooting outside the house quickly, quickly",

10:04.166 --> 10:06.200
I say "maybe it’s the army shooting?",

10:06.233 --> 10:08.500
"I hear shouting in Arabic".

10:09.600 --> 10:13.466
"Please bring someone, my mum is stressed",

10:13.466 --> 10:16.366
"she wants to know what's going on"

10:16.366 --> 10:19.100
"What about my brother? I'm so worried".

10:19.766 --> 10:21.300
At a certain point,

10:21.300 --> 10:24.966
her brother starts sending her messages,

10:24.966 --> 10:27.633
telling her that he's in another room at the kibbutz,

10:27.633 --> 10:31.066
with another friend and that they are in the safe room,

10:31.466 --> 10:34.666
there's a battle on the handle of the safe room.

10:34.666 --> 10:37.066
Because there are terrorists on the other side of the door,

10:37.066 --> 10:38.400
trying to break in.

10:39.066 --> 10:41.200
He starts writing,

10:41.300 --> 10:42.733
look who is,

10:42.833 --> 10:45.966
who is texting for help,

10:45.966 --> 10:48.333
his fourteen-and-half year old sister,

10:49.033 --> 10:51.466
and he starts telling her

10:52.266 --> 10:54.133
that he can’t hold it anymore,

10:54.700 --> 10:57.200
that if they will not send somebody,

10:57.500 --> 10:58.900
he's going to die,

10:59.400 --> 11:03.266
and at a certain point he gets completely crazy,

11:03.266 --> 11:05.200
just from the whole situation,

11:05.200 --> 11:08.033
and he starts writing her messages saying

11:08.033 --> 11:09.400
"Stop lying to me",

11:09.433 --> 11:11.266
"you’re always saying you'll send somebody",

11:11.266 --> 11:14.766
"Nobody is coming", and really he completely lost it.

11:15.166 --> 11:17.333
And this amazing brave girl,

11:17.400 --> 11:19.400
she sends all the messages to me,

11:19.766 --> 11:21.566
and she keeps instructing me,

11:21.566 --> 11:23.166
where the houses are,

11:23.166 --> 11:24.466
where they are at.

11:25.033 --> 11:27.400
I don’t know what to do.

11:27.400 --> 11:29.200
I'm trapped in my safe room,

11:29.766 --> 11:32.400
and I have no idea what's happening around the kibbutz,

11:32.400 --> 11:34.566
I have no idea who's alive,

11:34.566 --> 11:35.600
who's dead...

11:35.600 --> 11:37.800
I already realized at 10:00 in the morning,

11:37.800 --> 11:41.600
that this is a deadly scenario going on.

11:52.566 --> 11:55.000
I start writing texts. I think,

11:56.566 --> 11:57.700
Every person

11:57.700 --> 12:00.166
that might have anything to do with security

12:00.166 --> 12:01.000
on the kibbutz.

12:01.300 --> 12:04.566
And I start sending the messages like crazy.

12:05.900 --> 12:08.800
End of the day we realized that I was sending messages

12:08.800 --> 12:11.200
sometimes to people that were already dead,

12:12.100 --> 12:14.933
but with this texting,

12:16.066 --> 12:17.366
this girl,

12:17.366 --> 12:19.300
saved her entire family.

12:19.300 --> 12:24.566
The whole day she sent forces to her family's house,

12:24.566 --> 12:26.733
and to her brother's unit.

12:28.466 --> 12:30.433
10:30: "I'm stressed",

12:30.433 --> 12:32.700
"they are shooting all of the over the place"

12:32.700 --> 12:36.066
"They're in the house, the whole house is falling apart"

12:36.166 --> 12:38.900
"Send someone quickly Oshrit, quickly".

12:38.900 --> 12:41.366
"They're breaking in, they're inside the house",

12:41.400 --> 12:43.433
"my mom is about to faint"

12:44.700 --> 12:51.266
At this point, I send her a prayer from psalms for protection...

12:53.766 --> 12:55.400
Because that's all I can do.

12:58.566 --> 13:00.100
And I write "pray"

13:02.000 --> 13:02.800
"pray"...

13:05.366 --> 13:07.966
She's saying "my mom is not breathing anymore"

13:11.433 --> 13:14.100
"They are breaking things, they are breaking in"

13:14.100 --> 13:17.666
"We must keep quiet, we must keep quiet",

13:17.666 --> 13:20.766
"there are screamings, please help us",

13:20.766 --> 13:22.100
"Please help us"

13:22.100 --> 13:25.600
This goes on and on and on and on...

13:30.900 --> 13:33.200
We realized only later on

13:33.200 --> 13:35.533
that there were so many cries for help,

13:35.633 --> 13:37.633
from so many different people,

13:37.633 --> 13:40.666
that it was very difficult for the amount of

13:40.666 --> 13:42.933
üeople that were fighting the battle,

13:43.300 --> 13:45.266
to get to everyone.

13:46.200 --> 13:52.733
We had 14 people on the kibbutz,

13:53.166 --> 13:55.666
that were fighting the battle,

13:56.633 --> 14:03.333
Against 350 terrorists that came in,

14:03.800 --> 14:07.833
in a community that has less than 500 people,

14:07.833 --> 14:08.933
including children.

14:10.033 --> 14:14.133
our luck firstly was that

14:15.400 --> 14:18.733
They came in three different waves and not all at once,

14:19.866 --> 14:22.166
that the 14 people that were at the kibbutz,

14:22.166 --> 14:26.666
even though 11 of them were very trained soldiers,

14:27.366 --> 14:29.666
of course they couldn’t defeat them.

14:30.233 --> 14:33.966
The gap in the numbers is unbelievable,

14:34.166 --> 14:37.300
but what they could do was slow them down,

14:37.300 --> 14:41.200
and harass them. And every time someone called for help,

14:41.200 --> 14:44.666
they just used to go there and drive them away,

14:44.666 --> 14:46.133
scare them away.

14:46.666 --> 14:48.566
They managed to kill many of them,

14:48.566 --> 14:50.633
but they didn’t,

14:50.633 --> 14:52.100
they of course couldn’t,

14:53.566 --> 14:54.666
defeat them.

14:55.000 --> 14:59.600
So what they did was that they held this place until

15:00.200 --> 15:04.800
more reinforcement came around

15:05.033 --> 15:09.300
01:15 afternoon,

15:10.800 --> 15:14.200
01:15 pm, they came,

15:15.400 --> 15:17.866
there came more forces inside the kibbutz,

15:18.433 --> 15:21.400
and they helped

15:21.400 --> 15:24.800
the people from here to fight the battle.

15:32.700 --> 15:34.633
The second wave of terrorists

15:34.633 --> 15:36.700
came through the front gates of the kibbutz,

15:36.700 --> 15:38.933
which is closer to where I live,

15:40.000 --> 15:41.966
and they split to two.

15:42.100 --> 15:44.366
One went straight towards my house,

15:44.366 --> 15:46.633
and the other one went

15:46.633 --> 15:47.700
right.

15:48.100 --> 15:49.766
There was a row of houses,

15:49.766 --> 15:53.300
the first row of houses right next to the front gate,

15:54.066 --> 15:56.400
and they started the massacre journey

15:56.400 --> 15:59.300
throughout those houses.

16:00.200 --> 16:03.533
At that time I'm sitting with my children and my family,

16:04.266 --> 16:07.933
and I see my husband, he sat

16:08.100 --> 16:10.900
with a laptop and he turns it on,

16:10.900 --> 16:13.400
and I see him turn completely pale,

16:14.366 --> 16:16.800
and he signals me quietly,

16:17.000 --> 16:19.066
so the children will not be bothered,

16:19.366 --> 16:23.133
and what we see is unbelievable.

16:23.600 --> 16:26.533
Hamas had the GoPro cameras,

16:27.400 --> 16:30.200
so not only they filmed the entire thing,

16:30.366 --> 16:33.533
they live streamed it. And not only that,

16:33.700 --> 16:37.066
they live streamed it on the same families'

16:37.833 --> 16:39.433
social media.

16:39.433 --> 16:42.633
The families that they were just capturing, torturing,

16:42.633 --> 16:43.933
murdering whatever.

16:44.366 --> 16:47.033
They put it on their social media,

16:47.033 --> 16:51.600
so their friends and families could see it real time,

16:51.600 --> 16:52.933
What is happening to them.

16:53.766 --> 16:55.866
Which is really,

16:56.633 --> 16:57.466
really,

16:58.700 --> 17:01.400
A sick idea.

17:01.700 --> 17:05.766
I was a few houses from there and I see

17:05.766 --> 17:07.766
my neighbors and friends,

17:08.233 --> 17:12.600
the first video we see is of the Elyakim-Arava family,

17:12.600 --> 17:15.600
I'm not sure which one I saw first but...

17:16.066 --> 17:17.933
And we see that

17:19.066 --> 17:21.500
the family sits down looks terrorized,

17:21.500 --> 17:25.266
they were all around them terrorists,

17:25.400 --> 17:27.066
they had three children there.

17:27.066 --> 17:30.800
One 8 years old one 15 years old and one 17.

17:31.566 --> 17:34.066
Two girls,

17:34.066 --> 17:35.866
and the 17 year old guy.

17:36.100 --> 17:42.533
And what Hamas did was take the 17 year old,

17:42.600 --> 17:44.066
Tomer Arava Eliaz,

17:45.833 --> 17:47.933
A brave, brave young man,

17:48.500 --> 17:51.300
they put a gun to his head,

17:51.400 --> 17:54.066
and they told him to go around houses,

17:54.066 --> 17:57.100
knocking on doors, telling people to get out.

17:57.900 --> 18:00.433
Now he was a very brave young man,

18:00.433 --> 18:03.066
and we know for a fact that

18:03.066 --> 18:05.400
by the ability of knowing

18:05.633 --> 18:06.666
the surroundings,

18:06.666 --> 18:09.966
he managed to save a few families.

18:09.966 --> 18:13.666
He was just honored by the president of Israel,

18:14.366 --> 18:16.766
his memory was honored.

18:19.866 --> 18:21.700
At a certain point,

18:21.900 --> 18:27.100
he ran away from Hamas, he tried running away,

18:27.366 --> 18:31.366
his body was found not far from the front gate,

18:32.300 --> 18:36.800
we don’t know how exactly he died, but he died.

18:37.800 --> 18:41.566
The other members of the family,

18:41.800 --> 18:45.766
the father's body was found in the outskirts of Gaza.

18:47.000 --> 18:51.800
The mother and the two girls she was holding,

18:51.800 --> 18:53.800
according to the girl's testimony,

18:54.266 --> 18:57.500
she was holding them in both hands,

18:57.666 --> 18:59.900
telling them not to be worried or afraid,

18:59.900 --> 19:02.400
because they're together and she's going to protect them,

19:02.766 --> 19:04.400
and...

19:05.600 --> 19:08.300
that second she gets shot in the head.

19:09.833 --> 19:13.600
And, the two girls one 8 years old and one 15,

19:13.833 --> 19:17.800
are taken to Gaza as hostages,

19:17.800 --> 19:19.933
after seeing their entire family...

19:21.233 --> 19:22.033
die...

19:22.800 --> 19:25.400
And they are staying there,

19:25.400 --> 19:26.800
for two months,

19:26.800 --> 19:28.400
until the second hostage deal.

19:31.166 --> 19:33.566
They didn’t come back in a good shape,

19:33.566 --> 19:34.700
to say the least.

19:35.866 --> 19:37.766
The second

19:39.100 --> 19:42.866
Video that we see is of the Idan family.

19:42.900 --> 19:45.333
We see again the family sitting on the floor.

19:45.700 --> 19:47.533
Again, we see the father wounded,

19:47.600 --> 19:48.900
we think that he is wounded,

19:49.100 --> 19:51.166
but we realized later on

19:51.166 --> 19:53.000
that it was the blood of his daughter.

19:53.000 --> 19:56.300
Of his 18 year old daughter

19:56.300 --> 19:58.800
that was murdered right next to him,

19:58.800 --> 20:01.466
when she tried helping him protect,

20:01.466 --> 20:03.600
guard the door of the safe room.

20:05.066 --> 20:06.866
We can hear the brother asking,

20:06.866 --> 20:08.266
"but why did you kill her?"

20:08.266 --> 20:10.066
"She was just a child",

20:10.066 --> 20:12.400
and we didn’t know which of his sisters

20:12.400 --> 20:13.900
he was referring to.

20:17.900 --> 20:19.866
It’s a certain point,

20:20.400 --> 20:25.133
when Tomer Arava walked

20:25.766 --> 20:28.933
with the terrorists, he reached

20:28.933 --> 20:30.766
another neighborhood

20:30.766 --> 20:33.000
and he knocked on the doors over there,

20:34.100 --> 20:36.166
and he said to many of the people

20:36.166 --> 20:38.166
"Don’t come out".

20:38.766 --> 20:40.300
And then,

20:41.200 --> 20:43.200
one of the houses that he knocked on,

20:43.200 --> 20:46.466
there was Omri and Lishay Miran,

20:47.066 --> 20:49.966
and they are such good spirits,

20:49.966 --> 20:53.866
good souls, that they couldn’t hear a 17 year old,

20:53.866 --> 20:57.600
in that situation. They were with a baby and a toddler,

20:57.900 --> 21:01.433
and they decided to put their knives down,

21:01.433 --> 21:02.800
and open the door.

21:05.433 --> 21:06.500
They were taken,

21:06.833 --> 21:09.700
and put with the Idan family in the same house,

21:10.200 --> 21:12.866
and suddenly we see on the video,

21:12.866 --> 21:17.566
we see the Idan family also,

21:24.166 --> 21:24.966
Wow...

21:26.900 --> 21:28.366
And...

21:30.700 --> 21:32.866
What happens there is that...

21:34.100 --> 21:36.966
There wasn't a pattern of who they take,

21:36.966 --> 21:38.566
and what they do.

21:38.566 --> 21:40.266
Every scenario was different.

21:40.633 --> 21:44.400
So in this case they decided to take only the two men.

21:45.833 --> 21:48.700
Omri Miran and Tsachi Idan, the two fathers.

21:49.366 --> 21:52.066
They took them to Gaza Strip.

21:53.400 --> 21:59.200
We know today that Tsachi was dead since December 2023, probably.

21:59.833 --> 22:02.600
But since then,

22:02.600 --> 22:04.200
we got so many different

22:04.200 --> 22:05.866
contradicting messages from Hamas,

22:05.866 --> 22:09.700
so just think about how horrible it is for a family.

22:09.700 --> 22:10.800
"He's alive",

22:10.800 --> 22:11.866
"Now he's dead",  "now he's ...",

22:12.500 --> 22:16.200
it really a vicious

22:18.166 --> 22:19.100
warfare.

22:25.966 --> 22:29.000
Omri Miran, our dear friend,

22:29.000 --> 22:35.466
is still held captive in Gaza for over 700 days,

22:35.666 --> 22:37.300
almost two years,

22:38.833 --> 22:42.133
and we hope that he's

22:42.466 --> 22:44.500
as healthy as possible

22:45.100 --> 22:49.900
and we are waiting and praying to get him back.

22:50.100 --> 22:52.166
To get him back.

22:52.166 --> 22:55.233
And to get the body of Joshua Loitu Mollel

22:55.233 --> 22:59.200
back to his family in Tanzania.

23:01.266 --> 23:03.133
Ah, we pray for it.

23:07.633 --> 23:08.600
Anyway...

23:10.600 --> 23:13.366
I was in my house and

23:13.466 --> 23:15.733
my son is handicapped,

23:15.800 --> 23:19.333
back then he used to walk with a walker,

23:20.633 --> 23:25.366
And, the bombardment was so heavy that day, that we all,

23:25.366 --> 23:27.233
were staying in the safe room,

23:27.233 --> 23:30.133
and there was not enough room for the walker,

23:30.233 --> 23:32.300
and besides we thought that...

23:32.833 --> 23:34.266
There were many people,

23:34.266 --> 23:36.900
because we stayed so long

23:36.900 --> 23:38.766
in the safe rooms,

23:38.766 --> 23:42.066
there were many people who used a bucket or a bottle,

23:42.066 --> 23:44.066
if they needed to relieve themselves.

23:46.100 --> 23:47.633
My son couldn’t,

23:47.633 --> 23:50.533
he had to have his accessible toilet.

23:54.200 --> 23:56.333
So, we had to

23:57.566 --> 24:00.866
go out of the safe room a few times that day.

24:02.066 --> 24:04.300
We started thinking about

24:04.300 --> 24:06.466
what would be the safest way to do it,

24:07.000 --> 24:09.166
so we thought that if he goes with the walker,

24:09.166 --> 24:11.100
he will not have enough time to turn around,

24:11.100 --> 24:12.600
if he needs to

24:12.600 --> 24:13.933
come back to shelter.

24:13.933 --> 24:16.300
So we decided we’re going to throw

24:16.300 --> 24:20.033
the walker away for the day and every time he needed

24:20.033 --> 24:21.233
to go,

24:21.233 --> 24:26.633
we just grabbed him, each parent by one shoulder, and

24:26.633 --> 24:32.966
carried him to the toilet. "Operation Toilet",

24:32.966 --> 24:34.400
it was every time now.

24:34.400 --> 24:36.366
Every time like this took a few attempts,

24:36.366 --> 24:38.566
because the bombardment was so heavy.

24:39.366 --> 24:40.700
And there was even one time,

24:40.700 --> 24:41.966
that we already sat him down,

24:41.966 --> 24:44.533
and we had to grab him and run back.

24:45.366 --> 24:47.000
One of those

24:47.100 --> 24:51.266
"Toilet adventures", as I come back from them,

24:52.066 --> 24:57.200
I believe it was about a 01:45 pm.

25:00.466 --> 25:04.366
I go back with my husband and my son to the safe room.

25:04.366 --> 25:06.366
I'm about to enter the safe room,

25:06.366 --> 25:09.000
and I hear someone playing with my door handle,

25:09.566 --> 25:12.033
and in the window next to the door,

25:12.033 --> 25:14.400
I see the barrel of an M16,

25:15.600 --> 25:18.266
and of course the first thing

25:18.266 --> 25:19.833
I think of is to run away

25:20.966 --> 25:23.133
and close the door of the safe room and lock it.

25:23.866 --> 25:26.933
So there were,

25:28.033 --> 25:29.666
there was a person there,

25:29.800 --> 25:31.600
and he could see me in an angle,

25:31.600 --> 25:33.700
but he could see me if he went

25:33.700 --> 25:36.266
he couldn’t shoot me because the angle was too sharp,

25:36.266 --> 25:39.566
through the window like that, through the glass,

25:39.800 --> 25:43.200
and he sees me and he starts shouting:

25:43.200 --> 25:44.966
"IDF, IDF open up!"

25:45.400 --> 25:49.300
So I look at him and I do see that he has IDF uniform,

25:49.366 --> 25:51.633
but you can put on whatever shirt you want,

25:51.633 --> 25:53.400
and it’s my children over here,

25:53.866 --> 25:56.300
and I don’t know what to do,

25:56.366 --> 25:59.100
and I turn around again to go to the safe room.

25:59.200 --> 26:01.400
I'm right next to the door of the safe room,

26:02.166 --> 26:04.866
and then he starts shouting at me:

26:04.866 --> 26:05.633
"No please",

26:05.633 --> 26:07.500
"Please don’t go, we’re Jewish",

26:07.500 --> 26:08.933
"we swear we’re Jewish"

26:09.266 --> 26:12.866
and then I hear that there's a bunch of men outside

26:12.866 --> 26:17.700
my door and they start shouting Jewish symbols,

26:17.800 --> 26:20.700
so I know that they are from ours.

26:21.066 --> 26:24.400
They said "today is Simchat Torah",

26:24.400 --> 26:26.766
"we were supposed to do Hakafot in the evening",

26:27.166 --> 26:29.200
"we’re just in the middle of Hagei Tishrei",

26:29.200 --> 26:30.933
"we just finished Yom Kippur"

26:33.966 --> 26:36.166
And I try to think as fast as I can,

26:36.833 --> 26:38.066
should I trust it, should I not,

26:38.066 --> 26:39.500
what should I do?

26:40.000 --> 26:41.433
And then I get this idea,

26:41.433 --> 26:42.966
and apparently I wasn't the only one,

26:42.966 --> 26:45.400
there were plenty of people who thought of that,

26:45.766 --> 26:48.100
I asked them to pray. I say,

26:48.100 --> 26:50.666
"If you’re Jewish I want to hear a Jewish prayer"

26:52.033 --> 26:53.833
Because I thought it would be something

26:53.833 --> 26:55.866
that is very difficult to mimic,

26:55.866 --> 26:57.533
a prayer.

26:59.033 --> 27:01.366
And they started praying.

27:02.666 --> 27:05.000
And I open the door and until today,

27:05.000 --> 27:06.933
my husband laughs at me that

27:06.966 --> 27:09.533
my husband at my wedding did not get such a hug,

27:09.766 --> 27:11.900
I fell on this guy's neck

27:11.900 --> 27:15.700
and the first thing that we thought was "Yay".

27:15.700 --> 27:18.866
"The IDF is here it’s over"

27:19.866 --> 27:24.766
But we were so far from the truth.

27:25.400 --> 27:28.833
It wasn't the IDF as an army.

27:28.833 --> 27:33.833
The IDF as an army lost that day.

27:33.833 --> 27:36.866
It’s very difficult to comprehend it,

27:37.033 --> 27:37.700
trust me,

27:37.700 --> 27:42.600
for Israelis it’s even way harder to comprehend it,

27:42.666 --> 27:45.266
but the IDF lost the battle that day.

27:45.800 --> 27:48.900
The people who came were actually private people

27:48.900 --> 27:50.233
from around the country,

27:50.233 --> 27:51.466
who saw the news,

27:51.666 --> 27:55.766
and call their friends and came in

27:55.766 --> 27:57.833
and put on their uniform and their weapons,

27:57.833 --> 27:59.266
in huge groups.

27:59.266 --> 28:01.066
They were friends from the army,

28:01.300 --> 28:04.866
and they just came down in huge groups,

28:07.233 --> 28:08.600
to help.

28:14.400 --> 28:17.900
From that moment on,

28:17.900 --> 28:23.366
we stayed 12 more hours in the safe room with horrible,

28:23.366 --> 28:26.533
horrible battles going on all around us.

28:26.800 --> 28:29.166
The things that this girl,

28:29.166 --> 28:33.500
that fourten-and-half-year-old was telling me by WhatsApp,

28:33.500 --> 28:37.666
in the morning arrived to my neighborhood,

28:38.400 --> 28:40.033
and I can feel,

28:40.033 --> 28:44.133
it already started at 10:30 when the first,

28:44.266 --> 28:48.600
when the second wave of terrorist came

28:49.633 --> 28:51.133
into my neighborhood.

28:51.666 --> 28:54.100
There were plenty of stories in my neighborhood,

28:54.100 --> 28:55.466
there was

28:56.066 --> 29:00.666
an 80 year old man that said to his family

29:00.666 --> 29:04.800
to go to the safe room while he sat in the living room,

29:04.800 --> 29:09.000
Right in front of the big window to be seen first.

29:09.266 --> 29:12.466
His thought was, his plan was, that they will see him,

29:12.466 --> 29:15.800
shoot him and continue, and his family will be saved.

29:15.800 --> 29:17.600
And that's exactly what happened,

29:18.833 --> 29:21.033
they shot him dead,

29:21.033 --> 29:22.566
he was sitting in the living room,

29:22.566 --> 29:24.100
just in front of the window,

29:24.566 --> 29:28.833
acting as if he was reading the newspaper

29:28.833 --> 29:30.966
he was shot dead but they continued going,

29:30.966 --> 29:33.800
and they didn’t go after his family.

29:41.466 --> 29:42.266
Really...

29:44.600 --> 29:47.266
We hear, I can’t even...

29:48.866 --> 29:52.066
All you hear all day long are the explosions,

29:52.433 --> 29:56.300
and if there's something that I really,

29:56.933 --> 30:00.366
really hope that you will never hear in your life,

30:00.433 --> 30:04.700
is a rocket falling just 2 meters,

30:04.700 --> 30:05.800
3 meters from you.

30:05.800 --> 30:10.000
This is something that shakes your entire soul and body,

30:10.000 --> 30:13.366
and this was the noise that

30:13.366 --> 30:16.266
I couldn’t get out of my head for like

30:16.266 --> 30:17.666
a year and a half.

30:19.800 --> 30:21.666
Wow it was so...

30:23.700 --> 30:26.866
They launch the rockets right on the houses.

30:26.966 --> 30:29.500
The house behind mine

30:29.833 --> 30:34.000
was the first one to get hit by a rocket that day,

30:34.366 --> 30:36.700
and we were very worried about the family,

30:36.700 --> 30:38.300
that was there for the entire time,

30:38.300 --> 30:41.566
because they also didn’t have infrastructures,

30:41.566 --> 30:43.133
and they couldn’t communicate.

30:43.300 --> 30:46.866
I ended up calling the mother

30:46.866 --> 30:48.500
of the husband.

30:49.400 --> 30:50.666
She was abroad.

30:50.666 --> 30:51.866
Poor, poor woman.

30:51.866 --> 30:55.066
And I didn’t know that she's also from our kibbutz,

30:55.800 --> 30:57.466
and I didn’t want to panic her,

30:57.466 --> 30:58.433
I said like

30:58.433 --> 30:59.600
"No, everything is under control",

30:59.600 --> 31:02.466
I didn’t tell her that I was worried about them.

31:02.566 --> 31:03.966
End of the day they were okay,

31:03.966 --> 31:05.933
we sent the army over there to check.

31:10.366 --> 31:12.400
The other noise that was very,

31:12.400 --> 31:16.266
very significant that day was of the weapons

31:16.266 --> 31:17.166
Like...

31:18.033 --> 31:19.900
You hear it,

31:19.900 --> 31:22.933
we heard it 20 hours non stop,

31:23.433 --> 31:25.266
and that was

31:25.266 --> 31:26.900
a sound that was very difficult for me

31:26.900 --> 31:28.200
to get out of my head.

31:28.266 --> 31:30.733
After we were evacuated from the kibbutz,

31:31.000 --> 31:33.133
I think it was a month after,

31:33.266 --> 31:36.766
I was sitting with friends outside in the evening,

31:37.066 --> 31:39.466
and suddenly I hear that noise, that...

31:40.400 --> 31:43.233
And I just get up and I duck,

31:44.766 --> 31:46.066
And I look around me,

31:46.066 --> 31:49.666
and I see a woman walking with a stroller on pebbles,

31:50.033 --> 31:51.766
and I hear a battlefield.

31:52.400 --> 31:57.533
So that was really made me understand

31:59.233 --> 32:01.000
that it’s going to take a while,

32:01.566 --> 32:02.866
until that trauma...

32:03.200 --> 32:06.066
We were like zombies for quite a long time.

32:07.000 --> 32:11.800
One thing I remember very vividly

32:11.800 --> 32:16.533
is that

32:17.566 --> 32:19.766
when they said that they are going to evacuate us,

32:19.766 --> 32:23.266
it was around 9:00 pm,

32:24.600 --> 32:25.733
and we got a message

32:25.733 --> 32:28.766
saying that we are going to get evacuated,

32:29.100 --> 32:32.000
but they said do not get out of the safe rooms.

32:32.433 --> 32:34.366
Only when soldiers come to your house,

32:34.366 --> 32:35.266
and then you will have 2,

32:35.266 --> 32:37.400
3 minutes to gather things that you need,

32:37.500 --> 32:38.800
and you will go out.

32:40.033 --> 32:43.166
And, it was already 2:00 am,

32:49.300 --> 32:54.066
It was already 2:00 am and they still haven’t reached

32:54.666 --> 32:57.800
my neighborhood. Almost 2:00.

32:58.700 --> 33:01.100
and...

33:01.100 --> 33:03.300
the WhatsApp groups of the women

33:03.300 --> 33:05.266
were very active that day.

33:05.700 --> 33:08.133
So my neighbors and I,

33:09.066 --> 33:12.400
we had the "2:00 am pact", we call it,

33:12.966 --> 33:13.766
we said,

33:14.000 --> 33:16.866
we spoke on the phone, we said, okay,

33:16.866 --> 33:19.500
the people that are evacuating us,

33:19.500 --> 33:20.566
they don’t know the kibbutz,

33:20.566 --> 33:22.500
they don’t know who's in every house,

33:22.566 --> 33:26.066
and we need to make sure that nobody is forgotten.

33:26.600 --> 33:30.066
So we had a list of all the names of

33:30.300 --> 33:32.100
my closest

33:32.100 --> 33:34.066
neighbors.

33:34.066 --> 33:35.300
We said, if they get here,

33:35.300 --> 33:38.366
we vowed that if the army gets here,

33:38.366 --> 33:40.600
we make sure that they take everyone.

33:40.600 --> 33:42.866
I had a list: Katia, Ravid,

33:42.866 --> 33:44.100
Adi, Yochi...

33:44.100 --> 33:45.166
I had a list,

33:45.166 --> 33:48.200
I had to make sure that they are being evacuated

33:48.200 --> 33:52.133
when I was evacuated, and we all had that agreement.

33:59.400 --> 34:01.500
One thing that you have to understand is that

34:01.500 --> 34:05.500
we didn’t have a clue about what was going on.

34:05.500 --> 34:07.366
I didn’t know about the Nova (Festival),

34:07.366 --> 34:09.400
I didn’t know about, I had no idea,

34:09.400 --> 34:11.266
I was in my safe room,

34:11.400 --> 34:14.266
and apart from getting text messages,

34:14.366 --> 34:16.333
I didn’t know.

34:18.233 --> 34:20.600
They took us to...

34:21.033 --> 34:25.066
They found this place in the kibbutz,

34:25.066 --> 34:28.766
in one of the places in the outskirts of the kibbutz.

34:28.766 --> 34:29.966
Far from the...

34:31.100 --> 34:33.066
Far, farther away from Gaza,

34:33.400 --> 34:34.733
and they brought...

34:35.100 --> 34:39.400
They always brought about 50 people to that place,

34:39.400 --> 34:42.266
they brought a bus and

34:42.266 --> 34:43.900
sent them away from the kibbutz.

34:44.633 --> 34:47.466
So because it took it took so long,

34:48.400 --> 34:50.900
they started from

34:50.900 --> 34:54.066
the neighborhoods that were attacked

34:54.066 --> 34:57.066
a lot harsher than mine,

34:59.600 --> 35:00.700
it took us time.

35:01.400 --> 35:04.733
So they put us on a bus,

35:06.200 --> 35:09.033
they took us to a place called Mishmar HaNegev,

35:09.033 --> 35:12.200
which is about 40 minutes drive.

35:12.766 --> 35:15.166
The kibbutz was filled with bodies,

35:16.800 --> 35:22.866
and I thanked god for not taking me at 9:00 pm,

35:23.266 --> 35:28.100
but taking me at 2:00 am, so my children couldn’t see,

35:28.200 --> 35:33.066
it was so dark outside, so it was spared from them,

35:33.066 --> 35:35.866
that ended up to be a blessing.

35:39.600 --> 35:42.533
Horrible, horrible views.

35:45.800 --> 35:47.100
On the roads...

35:49.166 --> 35:50.500
Horrible views.

35:51.100 --> 35:53.200
I speak with a friend from Mefalsim,

35:56.366 --> 36:02.100
She gets out of her kibbutz to evacuate because

36:02.100 --> 36:05.100
they weren't evacuated because

36:05.500 --> 36:07.400
they were not the closest to the border,

36:07.400 --> 36:10.100
and they managed

36:10.266 --> 36:11.533
to defeat,

36:12.300 --> 36:14.033
they had much less,

36:14.666 --> 36:17.766
less terrorists came and they were able to defeat them.

36:20.100 --> 36:21.200
So people said "okay,"

36:21.200 --> 36:22.300
"Mefalsim,"

36:22.300 --> 36:24.266
"They got it going everything is fine".

36:24.433 --> 36:30.700
And then she drives out of her kibbutz and she's saying,

36:31.400 --> 36:32.800
she's saying to me:

36:35.400 --> 36:38.600
"Everybody is... It’s like a graveyard",

36:39.866 --> 36:41.900
And, she gets crazy she's going like

36:41.900 --> 36:44.166
"Everybody's dead, everybody's dead",

36:44.233 --> 36:47.366
She starts screaming,

36:47.366 --> 36:49.466
she calls her husband,

36:49.966 --> 36:51.366
and he just

36:51.366 --> 36:53.366
guides her on,

36:53.433 --> 36:55.333
he says "Step on the gas",

36:55.400 --> 36:57.233
"Step on the gas, keep on going".

36:57.233 --> 36:59.000
"Keep on going, you can do this",

36:59.266 --> 37:01.500
And she,

37:02.033 --> 37:03.966
her alone with her children,

37:05.600 --> 37:07.900
It was a horror.

37:07.900 --> 37:11.366
It was a scene from a horror...

37:13.000 --> 37:14.466
Not even a movie,

37:14.466 --> 37:16.566
it’s completely reality,

37:17.100 --> 37:19.166
and they...

37:22.833 --> 37:25.100
We were evacuated to Mishmar HaNegev,

37:25.300 --> 37:26.700
and I will always,

37:26.700 --> 37:31.900
in my life, remember, that in Mishmar HaNegev,

37:31.900 --> 37:33.866
they put some

37:33.866 --> 37:36.466
tea and coffee and some cakes for us,

37:36.700 --> 37:38.466
and in order to get to the hall,

37:38.466 --> 37:40.066
where everybody was gathering,

37:40.066 --> 37:44.633
I needed to take few steps and step down,

37:44.633 --> 37:46.300
go down to the place,

37:47.000 --> 37:49.000
I call it "The stairs of death".

37:50.300 --> 37:55.866
Every step I took I heard of another friend

37:58.566 --> 38:00.400
that I will never see again.

38:03.966 --> 38:06.866
It was the start of a body count

38:09.066 --> 38:10.800
that we had to

38:13.800 --> 38:15.700
to face and

38:15.700 --> 38:18.500
It was a very long one because

38:19.000 --> 38:20.833
firstly,

38:20.833 --> 38:22.500
there were people that we didn’t know

38:22.500 --> 38:25.000
whether they were kidnapped,

38:25.000 --> 38:28.466
or murdered brutally and we cannot identify the body,

38:29.633 --> 38:34.033
there were people from other kibbutzim that...

38:34.033 --> 38:35.800
There was this thing.

38:36.666 --> 38:38.066
Between everyone.

38:38.633 --> 38:42.966
We were scared of sending messages to friends

38:43.500 --> 38:46.033
from other kibbutzim. It took us

38:46.033 --> 38:47.066
3, 4 days.

38:47.633 --> 38:49.700
We were looking for lists,

38:51.266 --> 38:54.866
And, when we finally did send messages,

38:54.866 --> 38:59.033
it was more or less the same all around the region.

38:59.033 --> 39:01.800
It was "just give us a sign of life"

39:09.766 --> 39:10.566
Oh...

39:13.500 --> 39:15.066
Every message like that,

39:15.066 --> 39:17.033
that I got from a friend, was like

39:17.033 --> 39:17.566
"Oh my God"...

39:17.566 --> 39:20.033
"She's alive" or "he's alive".

39:20.033 --> 39:21.766
"Oh my God thank God"

39:26.200 --> 39:29.000
And every answer that I got,

39:29.566 --> 39:30.233
there were people,

39:30.233 --> 39:33.666
I didn’t have the guts to send a message to.

39:33.900 --> 39:36.466
I just waited for them to contact me.

39:43.400 --> 39:46.033
So, every day and for a long time,

39:46.400 --> 39:50.933
you hear, you’re going from a funeral to a memorial to a...

39:53.033 --> 39:55.000
To give your condolences,

39:55.000 --> 39:56.400
it’s just, we just couldn’t.

39:57.966 --> 40:00.666
The amounts were horrific.

40:07.600 --> 40:09.466
And, then it took us a very long time,

40:09.466 --> 40:10.966
to get back on our feet,

40:10.966 --> 40:13.666
I can’t even say that we’re back on our feet yet,

40:14.400 --> 40:19.033
I can say that very good people from Israel,

40:19.033 --> 40:20.700
and from around the world,

40:22.800 --> 40:25.200
really many,

40:25.200 --> 40:27.000
especially Jews,

40:27.000 --> 40:30.600
but not only, not only. Many people, Christians.

40:30.600 --> 40:31.733
Oh my God...

40:31.766 --> 40:34.033
We got so much help

40:34.033 --> 40:37.566
from Christians around the world.

40:39.266 --> 40:40.866
We were just

40:42.800 --> 40:46.133
embraced with a very warm embrace.

40:49.833 --> 40:53.566
You asked me earlier about

40:54.300 --> 40:57.666
the Israeli Muslims or Israeli Arabs.

40:58.033 --> 41:00.600
What happened then was that

41:00.600 --> 41:05.066
many of them came also to where we were evacuated to,

41:05.233 --> 41:07.800
And they came also to bring help.

41:08.166 --> 41:11.666
And when I said to one of them,

41:11.666 --> 41:14.100
there was one of them that came with a car,

41:14.266 --> 41:16.366
with a pickup truck,

41:16.366 --> 41:19.566
really filled with aid for us,

41:20.500 --> 41:23.733
and I remember that I said "Thank you",

41:24.300 --> 41:26.333
and he started crying,

41:27.200 --> 41:29.666
and he said to me "Don’t thank me",

41:29.766 --> 41:31.700
"It happened to all of us".

41:32.233 --> 41:35.100
"What happened to you, it happened to all of us"

41:36.033 --> 41:39.066
He said "Every peaceful person of the Middle East,".

41:39.300 --> 41:41.733
"every moderate person of the Middle East,"

41:44.500 --> 41:47.000
"It was an attack of all on all of us",

41:47.000 --> 41:48.900
"so don’t you say thank you."
